# Fast Verification Workflow

- Every behavior change still needs a relevant automated test, but run only the narrowest affected test file or test filter while developing.
- Do not run the complete PHP test suite after every small task.
- Run the complete PHP test suite only when the user requests it, a phase/checkpoint is complete, before a commit or push, or a broad dependency, authentication, shared middleware, database, or configuration change creates meaningful regression risk.
- For documentation-only changes, run `git diff --check`; do not run application tests or frontend builds.
- For PHP changes, run focused tests and Laravel Pint only on changed PHP files through `vendor/bin/pint --dirty --format agent`.
- For frontend changes, run focused linting for changed files. Do not run a production build unless entry points, dependencies, bundler configuration, shared application wiring, or a release checkpoint changed.
- Reuse a recent passing full-suite or production-build result when no later change affects its coverage.
- Report exactly which focused checks ran and clearly say when the full suite or production build was intentionally deferred.
- Never skip validation of authentication, authorization, payments, destructive data operations, migrations, or other security-critical behavior; keep those checks focused when possible.
